{:edb/db-before-t 1515 :edb/db-after-t 1516 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534828 50 #inst "2026-10-12T16:57:38.189Z" 13194139534828 17592186045417 true] [17592186102072 1078 #edb/ref 17592186102074 13194139534828 17592186045417 true] [17592186105900 1038 #edb/ref 17592186437253 13194139534828 17592186045417 true] [17592186105901 1038 #edb/ref 17592186437252 13194139534828 17592186045417 true] [17592186105902 1038 #edb/ref 17592186437251 13194139534828 17592186045417 true] [17592186105902 1038 #edb/ref 17592186437254 13194139534828 17592186045417 true] [17592186106031 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534828 17592186045417 true] [17592186106031 1071 "Find $E[X^{3} - 2X]$, given that the continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n$f(x) = \\frac{x^{2}}{9}, 0 \\le x \\le 3$." 13194139534828 17592186045417 false] [17592186106031 1071 "Find $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}-2X],$ given that the continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9},\\,0\\le x\\le 3.\n$$" 13194139534828 17592186045417 true] [17592186106031 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ and a function $r(x),$ the rule of the lazy statistician states that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X)]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nr(x)={x}^{3}-2x.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}-2X] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{3}-2x)\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{9}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{9})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{6}}{54}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{18}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{27}{2}-\\frac{9}{2}]-0 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534828 17592186045417 true] [17592186437228 1043 #edb/ref 17592186437255 13194139534828 17592186045417 true] [17592186437228 1043 #edb/ref 17592186437256 13194139534828 17592186045417 true] [17592186437228 1043 #edb/ref 17592186437257 1319413953482